[Music]  to make each inlaid cabinet door a  woodworker clues the pattern onto the  wood making sure that it's perfectly  centered  [Music]  then using a router he cuts about three  millimeters deep making a groove along  the patterns perimeter and cutting out  the parts that will be inlaid with  mother-of-pearl  [Music]  meanwhile using another copy of the  pattern a worker makes templates by  cutting out the same parts the  woodworker routed out of the cabinet  door each template is marked either pink  white or green she glues it into a three  millimeter thick piece of the  corresponding color of mother-of-pearl  [Music]  the next craftsperson takes one piece at  a time and holding it steady with pliers  carefully sauce around the template with  the one millimeter wide blade once she's  cut all the pieces she reassembles the  pattern the next craftsperson spreads  adhesive paste into the cutouts in the  cabinet door then he fills each cutout  with its corresponding piece of  mother-of-pearl five hours from now once  the adhesive has dried  he runs a sander over the design to  remove the paper and excess adhesive  smooth the wood and polished the  mother-of-pearl  [Music]  then an artist h-his fine detail into  the mother-of-pearl this provides  texture dimension and expression to  objects and characters which until now  were merely blank shapes  [Music]

